//? Title: Word CNN:real reviews and visible tensor Adadelta
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Genuine Pang/Lee movie-review snippets feed a complete random-embedding wide3/4/5 CNN. Explicit tensor SGD count references,all60 standard Adadelta updates,separate head projections and original held-out text reveal both computation and limited sentiment results.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.9_1d_convolutions/kim_sentence_cnn.cpp`.

> The method

Fit token vocabulary only on retained original reviews,keep PAD0 structurally zero,and pool parallel wide word windows. Show the ordinary tensor optimizer and post-step maxnorm projection explicitly. Restore nine learned leaves for words-and-lengths-only inference,then compare every held-out prediction with the unchanged SGD unigram reference.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/kim_sentence_cnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/kim_sentence_cnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/kim_sentence_cnn_concept.tikz > build/kim_sentence_cnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/kim_sentence_cnn_concept.svg build/kim_sentence_cnn_concept.dvi > build/kim_sentence_cnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
